{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-08-Jul-2024-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "A person borrowed some money at the rate of 8% per annum for the first two years, at the rate of 11% per annum for the next three years, and at the rate of 16% per annum for the period beyond five years. If he pays a total interest of ₹21,400 at the end of nine years, how much money did he borrow (round to the nearest unit) ?", "options": [{"text": "₹11,938", "added": false}, {"text": "₹18,738", "added": false}, {"text": "₹15,938", "added": false}, {"text": "₹18,938", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Let C be a circle with center O and AB be a chord of C such that the length of AB is equal to the radius of C. Let D be any point on major arc of AB. Find ∠ AOB and ∠ ADB, respectively.", "options": [{"text": "120°; 100°", "added": false}, {"text": "60°; 30°", "added": false}, {"text": "100°; 80°", "added": false}, {"text": "90°; 60°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "A’s marks in Mathematics are directly proportional to practice time. In 6 hours of practice, A gets 70 marks. What should be the practice time (approximately) to get 90 marks?", "options": [{"text": "8 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "8.3 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "7 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "7.7 hours", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "approximation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "Two circles of radii 16 cm and 4 cm, respectively, touch each other externally at Point A. PQ is the direct common tangent of these circles with centres C1 and C2, respectively. What is the length of PQ?", "options": [{"text": "15 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "20 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "16 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "18 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2 : 1", "added": false}, {"text": "1 : 4", "added": false}, {"text": "4 : 1", "added": false}, {"text": "1 : 2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "An interval of 2 hours 25 minutes is wrongly estimated by 2 hours 30.5 minutes. The error percentage is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "How many numbers between 10 and 65 are divisible by 2, 3 and 4?", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "A shopkeeper charges his customer 14% more than the cost price. If a customer paid ₹18,240 for a mobile phone, then the cost price of the mobile phone was:", "options": [{"text": "₹20,793.60", "added": false}, {"text": "₹15,686.40", "added": false}, {"text": "₹16,600", "added": false}, {"text": "₹16,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "₹5", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4.50", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6.50", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "A father is presently 3 times his daughter’s age. After 10 years he will be twice as old as her. Find the daughter’s present age.", "options": [{"text": "5 years", "added": false}, {"text": "10 years", "added": false}, {"text": "20 years", "added": false}, {"text": "15 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "In a triangle ABC, D and E are two points on sides AB and AC, respectively, such that DE is parallel to BC and AD : DB = 3 : 5. If AC = 5.6 cm, then find the value (in cm) of AE.", "options": [{"text": "2.3", "added": false}, {"text": "2.1", "added": false}, {"text": "1.9", "added": false}, {"text": "2.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "766", "added": false}, {"text": "756", "added": false}, {"text": "750", "added": false}, {"text": "700", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "If the radius of a sphere is increased by 5%, then by what percentage will the surface area of the sphere increase?", "options": [{"text": "13.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "11.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "10.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "15.25%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "The price of a car is decreased by 15% and 20% in two successive years respectively. What percentage of the price of the car is decreased after two years?", "options": [{"text": "32%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "46%", "added": false}, {"text": "15%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "A policeman is chasing a thief at a speed of 12 km/h, and the thief is running at a speed of 8 km/h. If the policeman started 30 minutes late, find the time taken by the policeman to catch the thief.", "options": [{"text": "120 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "60 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "90 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "100 minutes", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "early-late", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "The average of the areas of 2 similar triangles is 706.5 m2 whose perimeters are in the ratio of 6 : 11. What is 20% of the difference (in m2) in areas of both triangles?", "options": [{"text": "157", "added": false}, {"text": "149", "added": false}, {"text": "153", "added": false}, {"text": "164", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "The perimeter of a rectangle is 70 cm and its diagonal is 25cm. The area of the rectangle is:", "options": [{"text": "425 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "300 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "625 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "420 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "polygons", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "If the price of rice is reduced by 24%, it enables Alok to buy 10 kg more rice for ₹2,500. The reduced rate of rice per kg is:", "options": [{"text": "₹25", "added": false}, {"text": "₹50", "added": false}, {"text": "₹60", "added": false}, {"text": "₹75", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3,850", "added": false}, {"text": "385", "added": false}, {"text": "375", "added": false}, {"text": "3,750", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}]}